{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And you shall proclaim.</b> As in ״וַיַּעֲבִירוּ קוֹל בַּמַּחֲנֶה״ (Exodus 36) — a term of proclamation (Rosh HaShanah 34)." "<b>On the tenth day of the month.</b> From the fact that it says 'on the Day of Atonement,' do I not already know that it is on the tenth of the month? If so, why is <b>on the tenth of the month</b> stated? Rather, to tell you: the blast on the tenth of the month overrides Shabbat throughout your lands, but the blast of Rosh HaShanah overrides Shabbat throughout your lands only in the court alone (Sifra)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:08:14.412704866Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}